Z||000000||RossT||04-06-2001||11:59 PM||||I have had several e-mails about the type of headlight used on my friends lambo project:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005231.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005231.html</A> <P>here are a few more pictures and info:<BR>The headlights are a standard 4 headlight (round) system from a late 50's or early 60's ford pickup.  The headlight mechanism is actually turned upside down.  Because of space (shallow depth) concerns some modifications needed to be done to the back. The lights are a standard 6 inch diameter light from a 4 headlight system.<P>After Jason had the lighting system done, he found that the system from a Chevy PU late 50's early 60's would have worked even better. Apparently they are not as deep as the Ford set up.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image007_3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image008_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image009_1.jpg"> <P>I think Jason is a forum member now, so hopefully he will add or edit any info on this post.<P>||||reg||1
